Submission `submissions/bai-xundi-2026-11-external3/`: `external.csv` and `HOW.md`; the 9 arrays are in the new Zenodo record doi:10.5281/zenodo.24216385 (`arrays_genus2.zip`, `arrays_elliptic.zip`), together with the certificates and the build programs.

**Submitter (Rule 5):** Bai XunDi, gtorens@gmail.com, Independent researcher. ORCID 0009-0004-2432-5034.

**What it adds:** 9 covering arrays below the current table (main at 26270ec), from the genus-2 and elliptic two-block constructions of my preprint C (doi:10.5281/zenodo.24055371):

- CA(559147; 4, 42, 20) (was 559653), genus 2 over F_23, fused 3 times;
- CA(559149; 4, 42, 21) (was 559655), genus 2 over F_23, fused 2 times;
- CA(559151; 4, 42, 22) (was 771983), genus 2 over F_23, fused once;
- CA(559153; 4, 42, 23) (was 559659), genus 2 over F_23;
- CA(740387; 5, 26, 12) (was 1085303), genus 2 over F_13, fused once;
- CA(740389; 5, 26, 13) (was 742573), genus 2 over F_13;
- CA(2031612; 5, 25, 14) (was 3080172), elliptic over F_16, fused 2 times;
- CA(2031614; 5, 25, 15) (was 3080174), elliptic over F_16, fused once;
- CA(2031616; 5, 25, 16) (was 2097136), elliptic over F_16.

`builds_on`: `new doi:10.5281/zenodo.24055371`, plus `fuse-ckrs2010` for the fused arrays. The method is new; it is described in preprint C (Theorems 3.1 and 5.2) and in `HOW.md`.

**Why external:** the elliptic arrays are 109 to 115 MiB and the four t = 4 arrays are 56 to 57 MiB, above the 50 MiB limit. The two t = 5, k = 26 arrays (39.8 and 41.0 MiB) are in the same record and are submitted with the others.

**Hashes:** `sha256` is the hash of the canonical form, computed by `tools/external_array.py`. The files are byte-identical to the members of the zips (SHA256SUMS.txt of the record lists both).

**Local check:** `python3 tools/external_array.py submissions/bai-xundi-2026-11-external3 --threads 4 --budget-minutes 60` on main 26270ec, reading the same files from a local copy: PASS, 9 of 9 claims, all `exceeds_table` (7 verified in full, CA(559151; 4, 42, 22) and CA(559153; 4, 42, 23) screened). Before the deposit every array was also checked exhaustively with `ca_verify` (`verification_log.txt` of the record).

The arrays are released under CC BY 4.0 (Rule 4).

