`builds_on`: `cphf-smc2006`, `fuse-ckrs2010` and `new doi:10.5281/zenodo.23787051` / `new doi:10.5281/zenodo.23787053`, per row. The methods are described in those preprints and in `HOW.md`.

**Why external:** 28 files are 64 to 183 MiB, above the 50 MiB limit. CA(742571; 5, 28, 12) is 42.7 MiB, but with k = 28 it cannot be screened and its full check does not fit in 15 minutes on 2 threads.

**Hashes:** `sha256` is the hash of the canonical form, computed by `tools/external_array.py`. The files are byte-identical to the members of the deposit (checked against its `SHA256SUMS`).

**Local check:** `python3 tools/external_array.py submissions/bai-xundi-2026-11-external2 --threads 4 --budget-minutes 60` on main 0e0bf0d, reading the same files from a local copy: 20 of 29 checked so far, all PASS and `exceeds_table` (19 screened, CA(742571; 5, 28, 12) verified in full). The other 9 did not finish locally within my time limit; every one of the 29 was checked exhaustively before the deposit with `code/cacheck.py` of the deposit.

The arrays are released under CC BY 4.0 (Rule 4).
